<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16429" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἆσσον</span></b>  (
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄσσιον</span></b>  acc. to <i><span class="en">
			Eust.
			1643.32
		</span></i>), Adv.
		
			Comp. of
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγχι</span>:— <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>nearer,</i> esp. of hostile approach, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἆσσον ἴτ᾽</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.567
				</span></i>
			, al., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				748
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τείχεος ἆ. ἴσαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					22.4
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				1306
			</span></i>; simply of approach, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυναῖχ᾽ ὁρῶ στείχουσαν ἡμῶν ἆ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					312
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>El.</u>
				900
			</span></i>; of a woman, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥτις ἀνδρῶν ἆ. οὐκ ἐλήλυθεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					1306
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίφρον ἆ. ἕλκεται πυρός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Semon.
					7.26
				</span></i>
			: c. dat., <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				722
			</span></i>: with double 
				Comp.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕρποντι μᾶλλον ἆσσον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					1210
				</span></i>
			: 
				Sup.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄσσιστα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					6
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄσιστα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					5(2).159.17
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Tegea</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Michel</u>
				1334
			</span></i> (Elis, <span class="entity">iv B. C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> hence new 
				Comp.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσσοτέρω</span></b> , with or without
			gen., <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				19.506
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				17.572
			</span></i>; later 
				Comp.
			
			Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσσότερος</span></b> , 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγγύτερος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				878
			</span></i>: 
				Sup.
			
			Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσσοτάτω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.430
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Crin.
			</span></i>): 
				Sup.
			
			Adj.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσσότατος</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				6.345
			</span></i> (Id.).</div>
